---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="About"
  description="Poesis harnesses generative AI for an age of governed synthetic autopoiesis: systems that regenerate their organization under explicit, machine-operable governance."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="motto">Define the world in software; generate it.</p>
      <h1>Harnessing generative AI for an age of governed synthetic autopoiesis.</h1>
      <p class="lead">Poesis transforms organizations through generative AI and agentic capabilities grounded in standard systemic governance. We author the standard, build the engine and application that run it, and deliver the transformation around them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section section--soft">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Our mission</p>
      <h2>Governance that systems can act on.</h2>
      <p class="lead">The governance definitions organizations should build from and evaluate against have always lived in prose, scattered across wikis, compliance spreadsheets, and review boards that drift from reality. Our mission is to turn them into typed, versioned, machine-operable definitions and to ship the stack that contextualizes and harnesses generative AI. This is governed synthetic autopoiesis: systems continually producing and renewing their own organization without escaping the definitions, constraints, and human purposes that govern them.</p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section">
    <div class="container">
      <p class="eyebrow">Team</p>
      <h2>The people behind Poesis.</h2>
      <p class="lead">Poesis stack and services originate from a single thesis: systems should be programatically <em>defined and governed</em>, not merely prosed. That project is carried by three persons.</p>
      <div class="grid grid-2" style="margin-top:1.6rem">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="founder-head">
            <img class="founder-avatar" src="/clement-cazaud.jpg" alt="Portrait of Clément Cazaud" width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <span class="tag">Founder</span>
              <h3>Clément Cazaud</h3>
              <p class="title">Chief Executive, Product &amp; Architecture Officer</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Enterprise &amp; solutions architect, software engineer, agentic AI expert, and systems thinker. Clément has spent his career turning sprawling IT landscapes into coherent, governed systems: mapping architectures, leading transformations, and building the tooling that makes governance executable rather than aspirational.</p>
          <p>Poesis products & services grew out of that work and out of the agentic AI era that now makes it tractable: the conviction that the definitions a system must obey belong in software, where they can be versioned, reasoned over, generated and supervised from.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:.6rem"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/clement-cazaud" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the full track record on LinkedIn →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="founder-head">
            <img class="founder-avatar" src="/brahim-ben-helal.jpg" alt="Portrait of Brahim Ben Helal" width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <span class="tag">Co-Founder</span>
              <h3>Brahim Ben Helal</h3>
              <p class="title">Chief Growth Officer</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Brahim has spent his career bridging technology and business, helping enterprise software companies transform complex platforms into scalable commercial success. Combining deep experience in SaaS, AI, digital trust, and enterprise sales, he specializes in designing go-to-market strategies, product positioning, and commercial systems that accelerate adoption while aligning product innovation with market demand.</p>
          <p>At Poesis, he leads growth strategy, ecosystem development, and customer engagement, working alongside product and engineering to ensure the platform addresses real-world enterprise challenges. His focus is on making advanced AI systems understandable, adoptable, and commercially impactful, helping organizations move from experimentation to governed, scalable deployment.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:.6rem"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/brahim-ben-helal-50273856" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the full track record on LinkedIn →</a></p>
        </div>
        <div class="card">
          <div class="founder-head">
            <img class="founder-avatar" src="/hamza-abidi.jpg" alt="Portrait of Hamza Abidi" width="72" height="72" loading="lazy" />
            <div>
              <span class="tag">Co-Founder</span>
              <h3>Hamza Abidi</h3>
              <p class="title">Chief Technology &amp; Engineering Officer</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <p>Software engineer and architect with a track record of designing, building, and maintaining modern software solutions where performance, security, and long-term maintainability matter. Hamza has worked across the full stack — Java, Angular, API design, application structure, and code quality — on large-scale projects for Enedis, ING through BlueSoft, and the French Football Federation.</p>
          <p>At Poesis, Hamza drives technical vision and developments, and platform strategy. He ensures the product is built on solid foundations that can scale and evolve as the platform grows, turning complex business needs into robust, executable technical solutions.</p>
          <p style="margin-top:.6rem"><a href="https://www.linkedin.com/in/abidihamza" target="_blank" rel="noopener">See the full track record on LinkedIn →</a></p>
        </div>
      </div>
      <p style="margin-top:1.6rem"><a class="btn btn-ghost" href="/contact">Get in touch →</a></p>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .founder-head {
    display: flex;
    align-items: center;
    gap: 1rem;
    margin-bottom: 1rem;
  }
  .founder-avatar {
    flex: 0 0 auto;
    width: 72px;
    height: 72px;
    border-radius: 999px;
    object-fit: cover;
    border: 1px solid var(--line);
    box-shadow: 0 0 0 3px rgba(45, 212, 191, .12);
  }
  .founder-head .tag + h3 {
    margin-top: .5rem;
  }
</style>

